{
  "schema": "SPORTDB_COMPETITION_MAP_V1",
  "purpose": [
    "Pin discovery's competition names to Flashscore's structured refs, so",
    "resolving a league is a lookup instead of a SequenceMatcher guess.",
    "",
    "'country' and 'expect_teams' are asserted knowledge, hand-authored: a",
    "league's country never changes and its member clubs are stable for years.",
    "'refs' and 'verification' are NOT hand-authored -- they are written by",
    "scripts/simple/build_sportdb_competition_map.py, which enumerates that",
    "country's real competitions and keeps the one whose real season results",
    "contain at least two of the expected clubs.",
    "",
    "So the assertion comes from knowledge and the proof comes from the",
    "provider's own data. Name similarity is used only to decide which",
    "candidates to try first; it never decides which one is written. An entry",
    "with no 'verification' block is a to-do, not a pin, and the runtime",
    "ignores it."
  ],
